# Zetaris (DATA layer) — verified working rules for WhyTrace

Zetaris is the single SQL access point for every fact the agents use. Everything below was **run against our local Zetaris 2.4.3.1 on 21 Oct 2026** unless marked *unverified*. Reference repo for extra syntax: `zetaris/getting-started` (Apache-2.0), files `open_data/usl/sql/*.sql` and `docs/guides/zetaris-lightning-sql-companion.md`.

## Endpoints (local install, compose project `zetaris`)
- UI + SQL Editor: `http://localhost:3000` · REST: `ZETARIS_REST_URL=http://localhost:8888/api/v1.0` (never 8889) · JDBC `localhost:10000`.
- Containers: `zetaris-driver-1` (query engine), `zetaris-api-1`, `zetaris-ui-1`, `zetaris-postgres-1`. Named volume `customer-data` is mounted at `/home/zetaris/customer-data` in driver and API.
- Inside SQL, `localhost` = the Zetaris container. Our services on the Mac are reached at **`host.docker.internal:<port>`** (verified for REST and Postgres). The public internet is reachable (CISA KEV verified).

## Calling SQL from the app — `packages/adapters/zetaris.ts`
```
POST {ZETARIS_REST_URL}/sql-editor/sqls/run
Authorization: Bearer $ZETARIS_API_KEY
X-Org-ID: $ZETARIS_ORG_ID          # 1 locally
X-Request-ID: <uuid4>
Content-Type: application/json
{"queryId":"<uuid4>","sql":"<ONE statement, no trailing ;>","source":"SqlEditor","limit":200}
```
- Success: `{"headers":[...colnames],"data":[[...row as strings]],"total":N,"timeUsed":ms}`. **All values are strings** (`"3"`, `"2026-10-14 09:52:00.0"`, `null`). Cast in the adapter with the expected column types.
- DDL success: `{"headers":["Result"],"data":[],"total":0}` (or `registered`/`removed`/`json` headers for USL commands).
- Error: HTTP 400 `{"msg":"<Spark/Hive exception text>"}` — e.g. `[TABLE_OR_VIEW_NOT_FOUND]`, `LightningDdlParseException ... no viable alternative`. Map to typed errors; never leak the key.
- Latency seen: SELECT 0.1–2.6 s; CACHE of KEV ~2 s; first query after start slower. Use a 60 s client timeout; a hung FILESTORE/S3 registration never returns (we saw 300 s) — always set a timeout.
- `limit` caps rows returned; there is no paging API. Aggregate/filter in SQL.
- `sql_id` = sha256 of whitespace-normalised SQL, first 12 hex. Log every call to the trace: `{action:"query_zetaris", sql_id, rows, ms, status}`.
- `SAMPLE_MODE=true` replays recorded results from `data/sample/zetaris/<sql_id>.json` captured from real runs only.

## Lightning SQL rules
- One statement per request, no trailing `;`, fully qualified names. `DESCRIBE BY "..."`: letters, digits, space, `_ . - ,` only.
- Non-ASCII / mixed-case / reserved column names need backticks: `` `İçerik` ``, `` `Gönderen` `` (verified with the Turkish corpus).
- REST tables re-fetch on every query → `CACHE TABLE <db>.<t>` right after creating. Source JSON must be a top-level object; flatten arrays with `LATERAL VIEW explode(data) AS r` then `r.*`.
- Do not reuse the same explode/UNION view twice in one query (→ `MISSING_ATTRIBUTES`); use window functions.
- Not supported (verified): `SHOW DQ RULES`, `DROP LIGHTNING TABLE`, `DROP LIGHTNING DATABASE … CASCADE`, `DROP SCHEMASTORE CONTAINER`, `DROP SCHEMASTORE VIEW db.v` (form is `DROP SCHEMASTORE VIEW v FROM container`). `CREATE SCHEMASTORE CONTAINER` has no IF NOT EXISTS → treat "already exists" as success.
- Teardown that works: `DROP DATASOURCE <ds>`, `DROP LIGHTNING DATABASE <db>` (drops its REST/file tables), `REMOVE USL <usl> NAMESPACE <ns>`, `DROP NAMESPACE <ns> CASCADE`.
- Agents only run read-only `SELECT`/`SHOW`/`DESCRIBE` (guard rejects anything else). All DDL lives in `scripts/zetaris_bootstrap.ts` (idempotent, `--dry-run`).

## Registration templates (all verified)
```sql
-- Postgres (JDBC). Tables are addressed as <ds>.<table> (no schema prefix).
CREATE DATASOURCE auth_pg DESCRIBE BY "University identity and sign-in logs" OPTIONS (jdbcdriver "org.postgresql.Driver", jdbcurl "jdbc:postgresql://host.docker.internal:5433/authlogs", username "...", password "...", fetchsize "1000")
REGISTER DATASOURCE TABLES FROM auth_pg
SELECT * FROM auth_pg.signin_events LIMIT 5

-- REST (our mail-gateway mock on the Mac; returns {"data":[...]})
CREATE LIGHTNING DATABASE MAILGW DESCRIBE BY "Mail gateway events"
CREATE LIGHTNING REST TABLE deliveries FROM MAILGW REQUEST(endpoint "http://host.docker.internal:8090/mailgw/deliveries", method "get", response_type "json", http_encoding "URLENCODED") HEADER (user-agent "whytrace") BODY ()
CACHE TABLE MAILGW.deliveries
SELECT r.* FROM MAILGW.deliveries LATERAL VIEW explode(data) AS r

-- Public REST: CISA KEV (1,754 entries on 21 Oct)
CREATE LIGHTNING DATABASE KEV DESCRIBE BY "CISA known exploited vulnerabilities"
CREATE LIGHTNING REST TABLE catalog FROM KEV REQUEST(endpoint "https://www.cisa.gov/sites/default/files/feeds/known_exploited_vulnerabilities.json", method "get", response_type "json", http_encoding "URLENCODED") HEADER (user-agent "whytrace") BODY ()
CACHE TABLE KEV.catalog
SELECT v.cveID, v.vendorProject, v.product, v.dateAdded, v.knownRansomwareCampaignUse FROM KEV.catalog LATERAL VIEW explode(vulnerabilities) AS v

-- CSV files: Zetaris file store (MinIO images are no longer pullable — do not use S3)
--   shell: docker exec -u 0 zetaris-driver-1 mkdir -p /home/zetaris/customer-data/shared/whytrace
--          docker cp data/assets.csv zetaris-driver-1:/home/zetaris/customer-data/shared/whytrace/assets.csv
CREATE LIGHTNING DATABASE FILES DESCRIBE BY "Asset inventory and phishing corpus"
CREATE LIGHTNING FILESTORE TABLE assets FROM FILES FORMAT CSV OPTIONS (PATH "/home/zetaris/customer-data/shared/whytrace/assets.csv", header "true", inferSchema "true")
CREATE LIGHTNING FILESTORE TABLE phish_corpus FROM FILES FORMAT CSV OPTIONS (PATH "/home/zetaris/customer-data/shared/whytrace/turkish_phishing_dataset.csv", header "true", inferSchema "true", multiLine "true", escape "\"")
```
KEV pick for the vulnerable appliance: Ivanti Connect Secure `CVE-2026-104935` (added 2026-10-13); re-check at build time.

## Unified Semantic Layer (verified lifecycle)
```sql
CREATE NAMESPACE IF NOT EXISTS lightning.metastore
CREATE NAMESPACE IF NOT EXISTS lightning.metastore.whytrace
-- ONE request for the whole COMPILE (multi-table DDL, ; between tables is fine inside it)
COMPILE USL IF NOT EXISTS security_usl DEPLOY NAMESPACE lightning.metastore.whytrace DDL
CREATE TABLE identity (upn varchar(64) NOT NULL PRIMARY KEY, display_name varchar(128), role varchar(16), department varchar(64), mfa_method varchar(8), home_country varchar(2));
CREATE TABLE signin_event (event_id varchar(32) NOT NULL PRIMARY KEY, ts timestamp, upn varchar(64) NOT NULL FOREIGN KEY REFERENCES identity(upn), result varchar(16), ip varchar(45), asn_org varchar(128), country varchar(2), device_id varchar(32), app varchar(16), mfa_prompt_count int, via_vpn_appliance varchar(32))
-- one ACTIVATE per table; the SELECT's columns/types must match the DDL (CAST explicitly)
ACTIVATE USL TABLE lightning.metastore.whytrace.security_usl.identity AS SELECT upn, display_name, role, department, mfa_method, home_country FROM auth_pg.identities
-- data quality: PK and FK rules are generated automatically
RUN DQ TABLE lightning.metastore.whytrace.security_usl.signin_event
--   → rows [name, table, type, total_record, valid_record, invalid_record], e.g. ["upn","signin_event","Foreign Key Constraint","3","2","1"]
SELECT ... FROM lightning.metastore.whytrace.security_usl.signin_event s JOIN lightning.metastore.whytrace.security_usl.identity i ON s.upn = i.upn
-- teardown
REMOVE USL security_usl NAMESPACE lightning.metastore.whytrace
DROP NAMESPACE lightning.metastore.whytrace CASCADE
```
- ACTIVATE also works over inline `VALUES` and over JDBC / REST / file tables.
- Custom DQ beyond PK/FK: `REGISTER DQ` syntax is *unverified* and failed in the upstream repo; express extra checks (ts order, recency, UPN domain) as named SQL checks in `packages/adapters/dq.ts` and report them next to `RUN DQ` results.
- DQ results feed the agents: a finding resting on rows from a table with invalid_record > 0 gets a limitation line and lower confidence.

## Discovery (read-only, safe for agents)
`SHOW DATASOURCES` · `SHOW LIGHTNING DATABASES` · `SHOW LIGHTNING TABLES <db>` · `SHOW DATASOURCE VIEWS` · `SHOW NAMESPACES` · `DESCRIBE DATASOURCE TABLE <ds>.<t>`.
